'\" t
.TH PROSEFIX 1 "October 2026" "prosefix 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prosefix \- fix spelling, style, typos and punctuation in Markdown files, in place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prosefix
.RI [ options ]
.IR PATH ...
.br
.B prosefix
.RI [ options ]
.B \-
< in.md
.br
.B prosefix
.BR \-\-setup " | " \-\-check\-endpoint " | " \-\-doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prosefix
fixes spelling, style, typos and punctuation in Markdown files, in place.
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix draft.md
prosefix draft.md \-\-diff
prosefix vault/ \-\-check
.fi
.RE
.PP
The first rewrites the file, the second shows the changes without writing
them, and the third writes nothing and exits 1 if any file would change.
.PP
prosefix applies a fix only when it is always right; when judgement is
needed it asks the model; anything uncertain is listed for you. A fix that
is always right (a known misspelling, a space before a comma,
.IR "the the" )
is applied outright. One that needs judgement goes to the model with its
sentence and a closed set of choices, one of which is always to keep the
text as written, and is applied only when the model is confident. Anything
else (no model, the model unsure, or no single right fix) becomes a
.B review item
with its reason; see
.BR "REVIEW ITEMS" .
.PP
For each file prosefix runs two
passes in one process, with one model endpoint, one decision cache and one
change list. The
.B style
pass is stylefix's: one English variety (US or UK) and one style guide (spelling,
serial comma, numerals, abbreviations, dashes, quotes, apostrophes, ranges).
The
.B proof
pass is proofix's: line-ending and whitespace hygiene, mechanical errors, typos,
model-adjudicated fixes, compound words and comma placement.
.PP
Each
.I PATH
is a file, a directory or
.BR \- .
Files are rewritten
.B in place
(atomically, keeping the file's mode; a symbolic link is kept and its target
is updated; a read-only file is reported and left alone). A directory is
walked for
.I *.md
and
.I *.markdown
files, skipping
.IR .git ,
.IR .obsidian ,
.IR node_modules ,
every other directory whose name starts with a dot, and the project's
.B exclude
globs. Files named on the command line are always processed.
.B \-
reads standard input and writes the result to standard output.
.PP
Never changed: YAML front matter, fenced and inline code, link and image
targets, URLs, HTML, and Obsidian syntax (wikilinks and their aliases,
embeds, #tags, %%comments%%, ^block\-ids, the
.I > [!type]
marker of a callout, and $maths$). Quotation marks beside protected text are
curled according to their real neighbours. Prose that only resembles such
syntax (issue #42, C#, "costs $5 and $10", a "# Heading") is edited as prose.
.PP
prosefix is idempotent (a second run over its own output changes nothing),
faithful (applying every reported change to the original gives the output
exactly) and bounded (only prose changes).
.PP
Any per-file error (unreadable, not UTF\-8, not writable, bad settings) is
reported on standard error and makes the exit status 2; other files are
still processed. In stdin mode the text is always written to standard
output, the original if the file failed.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input and output
.TP
.IR PATH ...
Files, directories, or
.B \-
for standard input.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write one input file's result to
.I FILE
instead of in place. Takes exactly one input file, not
.BR \- .
.TP
.B \-\-stdin\-filename \fIPATH\fR
With
.BR \- ,
the path used for settings lookup, for
.B exclude
matching and as
.B path
in
.BR \-\-json .
Editors pass the note's real path this way. Without it, settings are looked up from the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Print a unified diff and write nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Write nothing. List the files that would change and exit 1 if there are any. Does not fail merely because no model was available.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the proposals as one JSON document (schema 1, see
.BR JSON )
and write nothing.
.PP
.BR \-\-diff ,
.B \-\-check
and
.B \-\-json
exclude one another.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
With
.BR \-\-check ,
files that have review items also count (exit 1). It is an error without
.BR \-\-check .
.SS What to do
.TP
.BR \-\-target " " {us|uk}
English variety. Without it, and without a project or front matter target,
each note's own spelling decides; see
.BR VARIETY .
.TP
.B \-\-style \fIGUIDE\fR
Style guide, as stylefix's
.BR \-\-style .
.TP
.BR \-\-only " " {style|proof}
Run one pass only.
.TP
.B \-\-skip \fITIER\fR,...
Comma-separated tiers to skip; see
.BR TIERS .
An unknown name is an error.
.SS Model
.TP
.BR \-\-llm " " {auto|ollama|none|cached}
.B auto
(the default): the configured endpoint, else local Ollama.
.B ollama:
local Ollama.
.B cached:
apply decisions already in the cache and never contact a model; items not in
the cache are left as written and reported.
.B none:
rules only; the cache is ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-url \fIURL\fR
OpenAI-compatible base URL. Overrides every configured url; see
.BR ENVIRONMENT .
.TP
.B \-\-model \fINAME\fR
Model name at the endpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISEC\fR
Seconds per model request.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Neither read nor write the decision cache.
.TP
.B \-\-require \fITOOL\fR,...
Exit 2 if any of
.BR vale ,
.BR languagetool ,
.B typos
or
.B model
is missing, instead of skipping what needs it.
.SS Reporting
.TP
.B \-\-changes
Print every change to standard error, one per line, with up to 12
characters of context either side, then the file's review items.
.TP
.B \-\-report \fIFILE\fR
Write one Markdown report covering all files.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only errors on standard error: no summary, no review items, no tip and no
lines about missing tools or a missing model.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Files processed in parallel. Default 4. Workers share one in-memory cache,
written once when the run ends.
.SS Configuration
These exit without processing input.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Choose, test and save a model endpoint (the shared adjudicate setup, for
prosefix).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-endpoint
Show the endpoint prosefix would use, where each setting came from, and test it.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Show which of Vale, LanguageTool and typos were found (or are missing, with the
command to install them), the endpoint check, and the settings file that
applies to the current directory. Exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit.
.SH FIRST RUN
A first in-place run (no prosefix cache directory yet) prints
.PP
.RS
.nf
tip: prosefix \-\-diff <path> shows changes without writing them
.fi
.RE
.PP
once to standard error. Nothing is written to remember it; it stops once
the cache directory exists.
.PP
Without Vale, LanguageTool or typos, prosefix still fixes the obvious
mechanical faults with the
.B basics
tier (see
.BR TIERS ),
and says once, in one line, how to get the rest:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix: most fixes need Vale and LanguageTool \(em brew install andrewbroz/tap/prosefix (or: brew install vale languagetool typos\-cli)
.fi
.RE
.PP
The parenthesis names only the tools that are missing. Without a model, one
more line says
.IR "prosefix: model decisions and comma placement need a model \(em prosefix \-\-setup" .
Other unavailable capabilities get one line per run (not per file), in the form
.IR "prosefix: skipped WHAT (WHY: FIX)" .
.SH VARIETY
When nothing sets the target (no
.BR \-\-target ,
no project
.BR target ,
no front matter
.B prosefix.target
or
.BR lang ),
prosefix keeps the variety the note is already written in. It counts the
distinct words, in prose outside code and quotation marks, that only one
variety spells that way (colour, programme against color, program).
Capitalised words, words in the accept lists and words both varieties accept
do not count, and a word counts once however often it appears. Two or more
UK words and at least twice as many UK as US words mean UK; two or more US
words and at least twice as many US as UK words mean US. Words of both
varieties without such a majority leave the variety spellings as written: the
spelling conversion is skipped for that note (everything else follows the US
default). With no such words at all, the target is US. The per-file line
says which:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix: draft.md: en\-GB (detected) \(pc 6 change(s), 4 for review
prosefix: draft.md: no clear variety (1 UK, 1 US words); variety spellings left alone \(em set \-\-target or lang: \(pc 1 change(s), 0 for review
prosefix: notes.md: no clear variety (0 UK, 0 US words); using en\-US \(em set \-\-target or lang: \(pc 1 change(s), 0 for review
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each file is decided on its own. To override, pass
.BR \-\-target ,
set
.B target
in the project file, or set
.B lang
or
.B prosefix.target
in the note's front matter.
.SH REVIEW ITEMS
A review item is something prosefix did not apply and you may want to look
at, printed as
.PP
.RS
.nf
draft.md:5: review \(em A comma may be missing after the conjunctive/linking adverb \(oqHowever\(cq. [proofix SENT_START_CONJUNCTIVE_LINKING_ADVERB_COMMA]
.fi
.RE
.PP
When the run's input is exactly one file (or standard input), its review
items go to standard error after the summary, also with
.BR \-\-diff .
With several files, each file's line counts them and the total line adds
.I (\-\-changes lists them)
when there are any;
.B \-\-changes
prints them after each file's changes, and
.B \-\-report
writes them to its file.
.B \-q
prints none.
.PP
The per-file and total lines go to standard output when the files are on
disk, and to standard error when standard input is read (standard output then
carries the text). Changes, review items, the tip and the lines about missing
tools always go to standard error.
.SH SETTINGS
For each file, prosefix looks upward from the file's directory for
.IR prosefix.toml ,
.I .prosefix.toml
or a
.B [tool.prosefix]
table in
.IR pyproject.toml ,
and uses the first it finds. Keys:
.TS
l l l.
target	"us" or "uk"	variety
style	string	style guide
only	list of "style", "proof"	passes to run (default both)
skip	list of tier names	tiers to skip
exclude	list of globs	files skipped in directory walks
accept	list of strings	words and phrases never changed
accept_file	string	file of accept entries, one per line
cache	string	decision cache path
.TE
.PP
Unknown keys and wrong types are errors naming the file and key.
.B exclude
globs are matched against paths relative to the settings file's directory;
.B **
crosses directories, while
.B *
and
.B ?
do not. A bare directory name does not exclude its contents: write
.IR templates/** .
.B accept_file
is relative to the settings file; lines starting with # are comments.
.B cache
defaults to
.I .prosefix/cache.json
beside the settings file; the comma decisions go to
.I commas.json
beside it. The cache, the accept file and the comma file must resolve inside
the project directory; a settings file that points outside it is an error.
With no settings file, decisions are cached in
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/prosefix/
(default
.IR ~/.cache/prosefix/ ).
Commit
.I .prosefix/
so CI can replay your decisions with
.BR "\-\-llm cached" .
.PP
The model endpoint is never a project setting; it comes only from the flags,
the environment and the user's config files, so a cloned site cannot direct
your key elsewhere.
.SS Front matter
A note may override the project:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix: off
prosefix: {target: uk, style: oxford, skip: [commas]}
lang: en-GB
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B prosefix: off
(or
.BR false )
skips the note (status
.BR skipped ).
The mapping may hold only
.BR target ,
.BR style ,
.B only
and
.BR skip .
Without
.BR prosefix.target ,
a
.B lang
of en-GB or en-US (case-insensitive; en-UK is accepted) sets the target.
Front matter that does not parse, or is not a mapping, is left untouched and
the note is processed with project settings; a
.B note
review item says why.
.PP
Precedence: command-line flags, then front matter, then the project file,
then the note's own spelling (see
.BR VARIETY ),
then the defaults (US English, the default guide for the target). Accept
lists are merged: stylefix's built-in list,
.IR ~/.config/stylefix/accept.txt ,
.IR ~/.config/proofix/accept.txt ,
and the project's
.B accept
and
.BR accept_file .
.SH TIERS
Each tier runs when what it needs is available; otherwise it is skipped and
reported once. Names for
.B \-\-skip
and
.BR skip :
.SS Style pass (needs Vale unless noted)
.TP
.B variety
US or UK spelling of the productive endings and VarCon variants. Vale.
.TP
.B guide
The style guide's word and phrase preferences. Vale.
.TP
.B ambiguous
Words whose form depends on meaning (licence/license). Vale; a model decides.
.TP
.B numbers
The numeral rule of the guide. Vale.
.TP
.B serial\-comma
Serial comma according to the guide. No tool needed.
.TP
.B abbreviations
Abbreviation forms (e.g., i.e., titles). No tool needed.
.TP
.B punctuation
Dashes, ranges, curly quotes and apostrophes. No tool needed.
.SS Proof pass
.TP
.B hygiene
Line endings, trailing whitespace, doubled spaces. No tool needed.
.TP
.B mechanical
Grammar and mechanical errors. LanguageTool.
.TP
.B basics
Needs nothing. A doubled small word (the the, of of) is removed; another
repeat (that that, had had) goes to the model, or is listed for review
without one. When LanguageTool's mechanical pass will not run (LanguageTool
missing, or
.B mechanical
skipped), basics also removes a space before , . ; : ! ? (not before ...)
and adds a missing space after , ; : between two letters
.RI ( analysis,design ).
Never between digits (1,000, 10:30, 3:2), in URLs, code or protected text.
.TP
.B typos
Misspellings. typos.
.TP
.B adjudicated
Model-checked corrections from LanguageTool. LanguageTool and a model.
.TP
.B compounds
Open, hyphenated or closed compounds. A model.
.TP
.B commas
Comma placement. A model.
.PP
With no model, the stylefix and proofix decisions that need one are not made
and are reported as undecided; rule-based tiers still run.
.SH JSON
.B \-\-json
prints one UTF\-8 document:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"schema": 1, "prosefix": "0.2.0",
 "endpoint": {"url", "model", "source"} or null,
 "skipped": [{"what", "why", "fix"}],
 "files": [{"path", "status", "reason", "settings",
            "changes": [...], "review": [...], "output"}]}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B status
is
.BR changed ,
.BR unchanged ,
.B skipped
or
.B error
(an error carries a
.B reason
and no
.B changes
or
.BR output ).
.B settings
holds
.BR target ,
.BR style ,
.BR only ,
.B skip
and
.B target_source
(flag, front matter, lang, project, detected or default), plus
\fBdetected\fR ({"uk": \fIn\fR, "us": \fIm\fR})
when the note's spelling was counted, and
.B variety_conversion
(false) when no clear variety meant the variety spellings were left alone.
Each change has
.BR id " (s1... for stylefix, p1... for proofix),"
.BR pass ,
.BR check ,
.BR start ,
.BR end ,
.BR line ,
.BR before ,
.BR after ,
.BR reason ,
.BR decided_by " (rule, model or cache),"
.B confidence
and
.BR depends_on .
.PP
.B start
and
.B end
are offsets into the whole original file, front matter included, in
.B UTF\-16 code units
(the unit JavaScript and CodeMirror use). A
.B line
is 1\-based. Standard input is reported as path
.B \-
or the
.B \-\-stdin\-filename
path.
.PP
.B depends_on
means
.I supersedes:
a change that lists others already contains their full effect over its span.
To apply a selection of changes, drop every change a selected change depends
on, then splice the rest into the original in descending
.RI ( start ,
.IR end )
order. Valid selections are closed under
.BR depends_on .
.PP
Each review item has
.BR pass ,
.BR line ,
.B kind
(undecided, rejected, alert or note),
.B check
and
.BR message .
Within schema 1 fields may be added but never removed or changed in meaning.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR PROSEFIX_LLM_URL ", " PROSEFIX_LLM_MODEL ", " PROSEFIX_LLM_KEY
Endpoint, model and API key for prosefix; below the flags, above the config files.
.TP
.BR ADJUDICATE_LLM_URL ", " ADJUDICATE_LLM_MODEL ", " ADJUDICATE_LLM_KEY
The same, shared with stylefix and proofix; below
.I ~/.config/prosefix/config.toml
and above
.IR ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml .
A \-\-url or PROSEFIX_LLM_URL drops the keys set in lower layers; set
PROSEFIX_LLM_KEY (or \fBapi_key_env\fR in the config file) alongside it.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama base URL. Default http://localhost:11434.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Replaces ~/.config. The accept lists and config files are read from it.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Replaces ~/.cache for the decision cache used when there is no project settings file.
.TP
.B PROSEFIX_NO_LT_SERVER
Set to 1 to use LanguageTool's command line for every file instead of one
local server for the run. Normally, when
.B languagetool\-server
is installed, prosefix starts it on the first file that needs LanguageTool,
on a free port on 127.0.0.1 only, shares it between all files, and stops it
when the run ends, including on errors and Ctrl\-C. If it does not start
within 30 seconds, prosefix prints
.I "prosefix: LanguageTool server did not start (REASON); using the command line"
once and carries on. If the server stops answering later in the run, prosefix
prints
.I "prosefix: LanguageTool server stopped (REASON); using the command line"
once, checks that file again through the command line, and uses the command
line for the rest of the run. For diagnosis and tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/prosefix/config.toml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/adjudicate/config.toml
Table
.B [llm]
with keys url, model, api_key or api_key_env, timeout, thinking_switch. The
first applies to prosefix only; the second is shared. A file that sets url
discards the model, key and thinking_switch of the layers below it.
.TP
.IR prosefix.toml ", " .prosefix.toml ", " pyproject.toml
Project settings; see SETTINGS.
.TP
.I .prosefix/cache.json
.TQ
.I .prosefix/commas.json
The decision caches, beside the settings file. They are written at the end of
a run, and only when a new decision was made; a cache that cannot be saved is
reported and does not change the exit status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.B \-\-check
found files that would change (with
.BR \-\-strict ,
files with review items too).
.TP
.B 2
A usage, configuration or input error, a failed write, a file that changed
on disk while prosefix ran (it is left alone), or a
.B \-\-require
failure. This wins over 1.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Ctrl\-C). prosefix stops the LanguageTool server, saves the
decisions already made, prints
.I prosefix: interrupted
and exits; files not yet written are left as they were.
.PP
A missing tool is never an error unless required.
.SH EXAMPLES
A first look at one draft, then the rewrite:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix draft.md \-\-diff
prosefix draft.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rewrite a whole Obsidian vault, listing every change and review item:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix vault/ \-\-changes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview a whole Obsidian vault, then rewrite it in place:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix vault/ --diff
prosefix vault/
.fi
.RE
.PP
A CI job that fails if any page would change, using only decisions committed in
.IR .prosefix/ :
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix content/ --check --llm cached
.fi
.RE
.PP
As a filter, with UK English:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prosefix - --target uk < in.md > out.md
.fi
.RE
